RNNoise, vendored for pw_denoise
================================

What:     RNNoise 0.2, noise suppression with a recurrent neural network,
          by Jean-Marc Valin / Xiph.Org. BSD-3-Clause: see COPYING, which
          has to travel with every copy, source or binary.
From:     https://github.com/xiph/rnnoise/releases/download/v0.2/rnnoise-0.2.tar.gz
sha256:   90fce4b00b9ff24c08dbfe31b82ffd43bae383d85c5535676d28b0a2b11c0d37

The release tarball, not the git tree: it carries src/rnnoise_data.c, the
trained model compiled in as C, which the git tree only downloads at
build time. Vendored so pw_denoise needs nothing installed and the AppImage
stays self-contained.

Taken: the ten sources of librnnoise's own build (Makefile.am,
RNNOISE_SOURCES) and exactly the headers they include, as `cc -MM` lists
them; COPYING, AUTHORS and README. Not taken: the x86 runtime-dispatch
sources (SSE4.1/AVX2), which librnnoise only builds when configured for it
-- the filters stay on the portable x86-64 baseline, so one binary runs on
every x86-64 CPU -- the examples, the training tools, the autotools.

No file here is modified. To update: replace these files from a new release
tarball by the same rule, update the version and checksum above, and check
pw_denoise's latency (denoise_dsp.h, DN_LATENCY) still holds: tests/denoise.py
measures it.
